Description: Fix m2m_changed_handler TypeError caused by enterprise removal
.
FIX FOR OSS BUILD: Required when building without /authentik/enterprise.
.
When Django ORM triggers m2m_changed signals (e.g., group.users.add(user)),
the thread_kwargs parameter is not passed and defaults to None. The base
AuditMiddleware.m2m_changed_handler attempts to unpack None with **,
causing a TypeError: "argument after ** must be a mapping, not NoneType".
.
ROOT CAUSE - ENTERPRISE MIDDLEWARE REMOVAL:
In standard authentik deployments, authentik/enterprise/audit/middleware.py
contains EnterpriseAuditMiddleware which extends AuditMiddleware. At line 130,
it initializes thread_kwargs = {} before calling super().m2m_changed_handler().
.
The base AuditMiddleware is designed to be called by EnterpriseAuditMiddleware,
not directly by Django signals. When we remove /authentik/enterprise for an
OSS-only build, the base middleware is called directly with thread_kwargs=None,
exposing this incompatibility.
.
WHY THIS FIX IS NEEDED:
Without /authentik/enterprise, the middleware inheritance chain changes:
  Standard: Django signal → EnterpriseAuditMiddleware (init params) → AuditMiddleware
  OSS Build: Django signal → AuditMiddleware (receives None directly)
.
The base AuditMiddleware.post_save_handler correctly handles None (line 207):
  thread.kwargs.update(thread_kwargs or {})  ← Defensive pattern
This patch applies the same defensive pattern to m2m_changed_handler.
.
This manifests as:
- Frontend: "POST /api/v3/core/groups/{id}/add_user/ 405 (Method Not Allowed)"
- Backend: "EventNewThread() argument after ** must be a mapping, not NoneType"
  at authentik/events/middleware.py:249 in m2m_changed_handler
.
Bug Impact:
- Cannot add users to groups via admin UI or API
- Cannot remove users from groups
- Cannot add groups to users
- Cannot modify permissions or roles
- All m2m operations on User/Group models fail completely
.
Author: Matthew Ramirez <matthew.ramirez@chainguard.dev>
Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/authentik/events/middleware.py b/authentik/events/middleware.py
index e53db33da..10ca867db 100644
--- a/authentik/events/middleware.py
+++ b/authentik/events/middleware.py
@@ -251,5 +251,5 @@ class AuditMiddleware:
             request,
             user=user,
             model=model_to_dict(instance),
-            **thread_kwargs,
+            **(thread_kwargs or {}),
         ).run()
